      "text": "The bug is that `execute` receives the raw QASM string instead of a circuit object. The fix parses the string with `QuantumCircuit.from_qasm_str` and passes the resulting circuit to `execute`.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import execute, Aer, QuantumCircuit\n\nqasm_str = '''\nOPENQASM 2.0;\ninclude \"qelib1.inc\";\nqreg q[2];\ncreg c[2];\nh q[0];\ncx q[0],q[1];\n'''\n\n# FIX: `execute` was given a raw QASM string instead of a circuit -> parse the string into a QuantumCircuit with `QuantumCircuit.from_qasm_str`, because `execute` only accepts circuit objects.\ncircuit = QuantumCircuit.from_qasm_str(qasm_str)\nbackend = Aer.get_backend('qasm_simulator')\njob = execute(circuit, backend)\nresult = job.result()\nprint(result)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
